 Challenges, Errors & Troubleshooting


❌ Issue 1: Missing Hard Drive During Windows Setup
The Problem: Windows Server setup threw an error: "There is an error selecting this partition for install". The installer could not see the virtual hard drive.
The Fix: The VirtualBox default SATA controller (AHCI) was not recognized by the Windows installer. I shut down the VM, navigated to Settings > Storage, changed the controller type to PIIX4 (IDE), and reattached the `.vdi` disk. 

❌ Issue 2: The "Press Any Key" Boot Loop
The Problem: The VM would boot to a black screen saying "Press any key to boot from CD or DVD" and then fail with a `BdsDxe` boot error.
The Fix: VirtualBox was not capturing my keyboard input in time. When starting the VM, I clicked directly inside the black window and spammed the Spacebar to ensure the VM caught the command to boot from the ISO.

❌ Issue 3: Windows 11 Black Screen / "Just a moment..." Hang
The Problem: After installing Windows 11, the VM would freeze on a black screen or hang indefinitely during the initial setup phase.
The Fix: This is a known VirtualBox bug with Windows 11 resource allocation. I powered off the VM, went to Settings > System > Processor, and changed the CPU count from 2 to 4. I also went to **Settings > Display and changed the Graphics Controller to VBoxVGA.

❌ Issue 4: Missing Host-Only Network Driver
The Problem: VirtualBox threw an error: "Could not find Host Interface Networking driver! Please reinstall."
The Fix: The virtual network driver was missing from the Windows host OS. I manually navigated to `C:\Program Files\Oracle\VirtualBox\drivers\network\netadp6\`, right-clicked the `VBoxNetAdp6.inf` file, and selected Install to register the driver.

❌ Issue 5: Explorer Freezing on Network Properties
The Problem: Attempting to open the TCP/IPv4 properties to change the DNS settings caused Windows Explorer to hang endlessly.
The Fix: I used `Ctrl + Shift + Esc` to open Task Manager, found **Windows Explorer**, and restarted the process. I also ensured that `Client01` was powered off while editing `DC02` to reduce CPU load on the host machine.

